    "title": "Why AEW Ditched Kevin Knight's Old Entrance Track Revealed - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sap Sinha ,\n30 minutes ago\nKevin Knight has switched up his entrance music, and fans now know why. The AEW star previously walked to the ring using Monteasy’s song “The Jet,” but after he turned heel and joined the Don Callis Family, he began using a new track called “Final Approach,” made by Mikey Rukus and featuring SayItAintTone.\nREAD MORE: WWE Star Praises AEW Wrestler For Transitioning Himself\nREAD MORE: Tony Khan Explains AEW’s Title Match TV Strategy, Nick Offerman Lands Emmy Nomination\nA fan asked about the change during a recent Fightful Select Q&A session, and Sean Ross Sapp answered with some helpful details. He explained that people within AEW simply felt the new song matched Knight’s current character better than his old one did. Sapp also made it clear there is no bad blood between AEW and Monteasy over this switch, since the artist still has plenty of friends within the company.\nKnight’s heel turn happened at AEW Double Or Nothing 2026, where he attacked Darby Allin right after Allin lost the AEW World Championship to MJF. Allin later called Knight out for a TNT Championship match during Dynamite, but Don Callis quickly shut that idea down.",
